prefix_rule(pattern=["/usr/bin/bash", "-lc", "git tag -f -a v0.2.0 -m \"Checkpoint Constellation\" HEAD && git push origin v0.2.0 && gh release create v0.2.0 --repo linsalrob/contigger --title \"Checkpoint Constellation ✨\" --target main --notes $'## Checkpoint Constellation ✨\\n\\nContigger 0.2.0 brings safer scaling and resumable merge alignment workflows.\\n\\n### Highlights\\n\\n- Bounded, indexed selective minimap2 alignment batches.\\n- Atomic relationship checkpoints that can be reused safely on retries.\\n- Checkpoint validation against canonical catalogue content and normalized configuration.\\n- Checkpoint invalidation across minimap2 versions and relationship-classifier revisions.\\n- Completion markers and decision counts prevent truncated checkpoint reuse.\\n- Strict validation rejects malformed, non-integral, non-finite, and oversized numeric fields.\\n- Updated performance, merge, and milestone documentation.\\n\\n### Safety\\n\\nContigger remains conservative: ambiguous, conflicting, or unsupported relationships are deferred rather than forced into biological joins.\\n\\n### Validation\\n\\nThe release is based on merged PR #37 and PR #38. CI passed on Python 3.11, 3.12, and 3.13, with strict documentation builds and benchmark validation.'"], decision="allow")
